## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:**track_time_taken_to_solve_puzzle**
```pseudocode
IMPORT pygame

CLASS Timer
    FUNCTION __init__()
        INITIALIZE start_time to 0
        INITIALIZE elapsed_time to 0

    FUNCTION start()
        SET start_time to current time in milliseconds using pygame.time.get_ticks()

    FUNCTION stop()
        SET elapsed_time to current time minus start_time in milliseconds

    FUNCTION get_time()
        CALCULATE seconds from elapsed_time by dividing by 1000
        RETURN formatted string in "MM:SS" format

CLASS Game
    FUNCTION start_game()
        CALL load_puzzle() to initialize the puzzle
        CALL timer.start() to begin timing

    FUNCTION timer_method_flow()    -- Representing timer functionalities
        CALL timer.start()
        // Simulate gameplay and puzzle solving
        CALL timer.stop()  // To stop the timer

    FUNCTION get_time_taken()
        RETURN timer.get_time()
```
